% What a program needs to state properties checked by elpi-check.
%
%   accumulate property.     % elpi-check puts this directory in the path;
%                            % with plain elpi: elpi -I elpi-tools/check/lib
%
% See elpi-tools/check/README.md.

% [property Name Formula]: Formula should hold.  elpi-check tests it on
% random values of its variables.
%
%   Formula ::= pi X\ Formula         X is a variable of the property: its
%                                     value is generated from its type, or
%                                     computed by a premise (an output)
%             | Premise ==> Formula   a premise (the test is discarded when
%                                     it has no solution)
%             | Goal                  the conclusion, checked for every
%                                     solution of the premises
%
% The type of a variable is inferred from the signatures of the predicates
% it is given to, or written: pi L : list int \ ...
pred property o:string, o:(pred).

% [generated-by G]: a premise whose variables are generated by solving G
% with random choices among the rules of its predicates, instead of being
% generated from their types: for the values that satisfy G, such as the
% well-typed terms of a typing relation.  Run as a goal, it is G.
pred generated-by i:(pred).
generated-by G :- G.
